building MCP server in python: refer to the project in repo MCP-STDIO
choice 1: STDIO
in terminal: 
$ curl -LsSf http://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh        //install uv
$ uv init .
$ uv venv        //create virtual environment
copy 'source .venv/bin/activate' in output and run $ source .venv/bin/activate
$ python main.py       //verify

open the project in VScode which has been initialised above, update main.py as below:
from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP        //library

mcp = FastMCP("add_integers")

@mcp.tool()
def add_integers(a: int, b: int) -> int:
    """
    Adds two integers and returns the sum.

    Args:
        a: First integer
        b: Second integer

    Returns:
        The sum of a and b.
    """
    return a + b

if __name__ == "__main__":
    mcp.run(transport="stdio")

terminal in VScode: 
$ uv add "mcp[cli]"               //set up this as a MCP server that runs from the command line
$ uv run mcp dev main.py          //run a developer server, it opens a browser page where MCP server is running to test tools
click Tools, it will show 'add_ integers' tool in the list, click 'add_ integers', it will show the tool where we can fill in value a and b to test the tool.

